# game/story/chapter2.rpy:20
translate indonesian chapter2_start_b44a8e20:

    # narrator "By nine o'clock, the Crooked Lantern's back parlor has been requisitioned into an impromptu war-room. Outside, Ashen Vigil sentries pace the wet cobbles in disciplined pairs."
    narrator "Menjelang pukul sembilan malam, ruang belakang Penginapan Lentera Bengkok disulap jadi ruang rapat darurat. Di luar, para prajurit Penjaga Abu berpatroli berpasangan dengan langkah tegap di atas jalanan batu yang basah."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:27
translate indonesian chapter2_start_4b5a6362:

    # cassian "Look at the survey charcoal, Broker Kael. I am not here to arrest you for an unlicensed Recall, nor to fine Master Sato for his... unusual footwear."
    cassian "Lihatlah peta arang ini, Pialang Kael. Aku datang bukan untuk menangkapmu atas pemulangan tanpa izin, bukan pula untuk mendenda Tuan Sato karena... alas kakinya yang tak biasa itu."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:28
translate indonesian chapter2_start_30a882bb:

    # narrator "High Marshal Cassian Vey unrolls a salt-stained map of northern Cindervale. His voice isn't booming or theatrical; he sounds like an ER surgeon on hour thirty-six."
    narrator "Panglima Agung Cassian Vey membentangkan peta Cindervale utara yang bernoda garam. Suaranya tidak membentak ataupun berlebihan; dia terdengar lelah bagai dokter bedah gawat darurat di jam ke-36 dinasnya."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:29
translate indonesian chapter2_start_bffd9295:

    # cassian "Twenty years ago, I carried the Sixth Paragon's shield to Fort Bastion. I watched a nineteen-year-old boy from Osaka pour every memory in his skull into that cliffside so thirty thousand refugees could live."
    cassian "Dua puluh tahun lalu, aku memanggul perisai Paragon Keenam menuju Benteng Bastion. Kusaksikan sendiri seorang pemuda sembilan belas tahun asal Osaka menguras seluruh ingatan di kepalanya ke tebing itu demi menyelamatkan tiga puluh ribu pengungsi."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:30
translate indonesian chapter2_start_5db89273:

    # cassian "Tonight, that seal is failing. If the Hollow Tide breaks into the valley before winter, Thornwick and six charter villages vanish."
    cassian "Malam ini, segel itu mulai runtuh. Jika Gelombang Hampa menjebol lembah sebelum musim dingin tiba, Thornwick dan enam desa sekitarnya akan musnah."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:32
translate indonesian chapter2_start_85b6ffda:

    # vespera "And your brilliant solution from the Eastern Choir is to march {i}another{/i} twenty-one-year-old into the Crucible of Crowns?!"
    vespera "Dan solusi hebat kalian dari Paduan Suara Timur adalah menggiring {i}satu lagi{/i} anak umur dua puluh satu tahun masuk ke Kawah Mahkota?!"

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:33
translate indonesian chapter2_start_a246e6cf:

    # vespera "Look at Envoy Lin's hands, Marshal! Tell me she isn't already fraying!"
    vespera "Lihat tangan Utusan Lin, Panglima! Coba katakan padaku kalau dia belum mulai terurai!"

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:36
translate indonesian chapter2_start_5db37bf5:

    # sera "Keep my hands out of your mouth, salt-smuggler. Unlike your desk-clerk mistake over there, I actually {i}chose{/i} to answer when Aurelia called."
    sera "Nggak usah bawa-bawa tanganku, dasar penyelundup garam. Nggak kayak anak kantoran hasil salah cidukmu itu, aku bener-bener {i}memilih{/i} untuk menjawab panggilan Aurelia."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:38
translate indonesian chapter2_start_6827a6a4:

    # narrator "Seraphina reaches for a pewter mug of Master Orin's hot herbal water, pauses, and frowns faintly at the saucer."
    narrator "Seraphina meraih cangkir timah berisi seduhan herbal hangat racikan Kakek Orin, terhenti sejenak, lalu mengernyit bingung menatap lepeknya."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:39
translate indonesian chapter2_start_08206804:

    # sera "Innkeeper—do you have a slice of... of that sour yellow citrus? From home. Round, dimpled peel, goes in hot tea when your throat hurts..."
    sera "Pemilik kedai—apa punya seiris... buah sitrus kuning yang kecut itu? Yang dari kampung halaman. Bentuknya bulat, kulitnya agak kasar, biasa dicampur ke teh panas kalau lagi sakit tenggorokan..."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:42
translate indonesian chapter2_start_18734d99:

    # narrator "Silence drops over the table like lead."
    narrator "Meja itu seketika hening mencekam."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:43
translate indonesian chapter2_start_9cb8dc7c:

    # narrator "Her fingers tighten around the porcelain handle until her knuckles blanch. Beside her collar, two tiny motes of silver Starlight flicker—and vanish."
    narrator "Jari-jarinya mencengkeram gagang cangkir porselen semakin erat hingga buku-buku jarinya memucat tegang. Di dekat kerah bajunya, dua butir cahaya bintang keperakan berkedip redup—lalu padam."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:45
translate indonesian chapter2_start_7db884a3:

    # thought "She just forgot the word 'lemon.' She's twenty-one years old, speaking English, and the magic literally ate the word 'lemon' out of her head."
    thought "Dia baru saja melupakan kata 'lemon.' Umurnya baru dua puluh satu tahun, kami berbicara dalam bahasa Inggris, dan sihir dunia ini baru saja melahap kata 'lemon' dari ingatannya."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:47
translate indonesian chapter2_start_3f85840b:

    # sera "...Never mind. Plain water is fine."
    sera "...Nggak apa-apa deh. Air putih biasa aja cukup."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:54
translate indonesian chapter2_start_ad8ef2b5:

    # leo "Lemon, Seraphina. Usually the plastic squeeze bottle shaped like one because real lemons go moldy in the crisper drawer."
    leo "Lemon, Seraphina. Biasanya yang dalam botol plastik pencet berbentuk buahnya, soalnya lemon asli cepat berjamur kalau kelamaan di laci kulkas."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:55
translate indonesian chapter2_start_4eac5215:

    # narrator "For half a heartbeat, Seraphina stares at me like a drowning swimmer spotting a pier—before her chin snaps back up."
    narrator "Sepersekian detik, Seraphina menatapku bagai perenang yang nyaris tenggelam melihat pelampung—sebelum dagunya buru-buru kembali terangkat angkuh."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:57
translate indonesian chapter2_start_5b28d5fc:

    # sera "...Right. Lemon. Obviously. I've been speaking High Aurelian all week."
    sera "...Iya, tentu saja. Lemon. Maksudku itu tadi. Seminggu ini aku cuma bicara bahasa Aurelia Tinggi."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:64
translate indonesian chapter2_start_33a507b4:

    # cassian "Do you think I sleep well, Master Sato? My late brother's eight-year-old daughter lives in Bastion Ward Three. Tell me what math saves both Envoy Lin {i}and{/i} thirty thousand sleeping families, and I will kneel to you myself."
    cassian "Kau pikir aku bisa tidur nyenyak, Tuan Sato? Putri mendiang saudaraku yang baru delapan tahun tinggal di Bastion Blok Tiga. Tunjukkan padaku rumus yang bisa menyelamatkan Utusan Lin {i}sekaligus{/i} tiga puluh ribu keluarga yang sedang tidur lelap itu, dan aku sendiri yang akan bersujud di hadapanmu."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:71
translate indonesian chapter2_start_ea8e8b37:

    # vespera "Give the clerk a gold star. If we had the First Era's Original Calibration Plate from the Sunken Archive, a distributed copper array {i}could{/i} bleed pressure off the Crucible without cooking a human brain."
    vespera "Bocah kantoran ini ada benarnya. Kalau kita punya Pelat Kalibrasi Asli Era Pertama dari Arsip Tenggelam, susunan konduktor tembaga {i}bisa{/i} membuang tekanan Kawah tanpa perlu membakar habis otak manusia."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:74
translate indonesian chapter2_start_333809ce:

    # cassian "The Sunken Archive beneath the Salt Wastes has been sealed since the Fourth Dawn. Yet... the Vigil requires dawn until noon to reinforce the outer Causeway."
    cassian "Arsip Tenggelam di bawah Padang Garam telah disegel sejak Fajar Keempat. Tapi... pasukanku butuh waktu dari fajar hingga siang untuk memperkuat jembatan luar."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:75
translate indonesian chapter2_start_1efa14b2:

    # cassian "You have twenty-four hours, Broker Kael. Bring me working First-Era proof from beneath the salt—or at tomorrow's twilight bell, Envoy Lin and I ascend the Spire."
    cassian "Kau punya waktu dua puluh empat jam, Pialang Kael. Bawakan aku bukti peninggalan Era Pertama dari bawah garam itu—atau saat lonceng senja berdentang besok, Utusan Lin dan aku akan mendaki Menara."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:96
translate indonesian chapter2_start_92f4850b:

    # narrator "Near midnight, unable to sleep on the inn's straw cot, I step out behind the Conservatory eaves—and nearly walk straight into a rapier-thin beam of cold starlight."
    narrator "Mendekati tengah malam, susah tidur di atas kasur jerami kedai, aku melangkah keluar di balik emperan Konservatori—dan hampir saja menabrak seberkas sinar bintang yang setipis bilah pedang."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:102
translate indonesian chapter2_start_458df410:

    # narrator "Seraphina stands barefoot on the wet flagstones, running sword-forms at punishing speed. A thin ribbon of luminous silver dust drips from her nostril; she wipes it furiously on her sleeve before turning."
    narrator "Seraphina berdiri bertelanjang kaki di atas jalan setapak yang basah, melatih jurus pedangnya dengan kecepatan luar biasa. Setitik serbuk perak bercahaya menetes dari hidungnya; dia buru-buru menyekanya ke lengan baju sebelum berbalik."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:104
translate indonesian chapter2_start_f617e0d6:

    # sera "Do they not teach knocking in whatever cubicle farm Vespera dragged you from?"
    sera "Memangnya di kantor kubikel tempat Vespera nyeret kau nggak diajarin ngetuk pintu dulu?"

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:105
translate indonesian chapter2_start_a8c04d0c:

    # leo "Technically there isn't a door out here. You're bleeding... glitter."
    leo "Secara teknis di luar sini nggak ada pintunya sih. Hidungmu... berdarah kerlap-kerlip."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:108
translate indonesian chapter2_start_049bf2b6:

    # sera "It's calcified ether. Happens when you hold three provincial wards up while half the Concordat Senate argues over wine tariffs."
    sera "Itu eter yang membatu. Biasa kejadian kalau kau harus nahan tiga pelindung wilayah sendirian sementara separuh Senat Konkordat asyik debat tarif pajak anggur."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:109
translate indonesian chapter2_start_175b106d:

    # narrator "She lowers her practice blade, breathing hard, and looks through the steamed glass at Master Orin's patch of ordinary green clover."
    narrator "Dia menurunkan pedang latihannya, napasnya terengah-engah, lalu menatap melalui kaca berembun ke arah petak rumput semanggi hijau biasa milik Kakek Orin."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:110
translate indonesian chapter2_start_9e1d3e27:

    # sera "Back home—Chicago, I think it was Chicago, near a big cold lake—I got a 99.4 average, first chair violin, early admission. And the one semester I burned out and dropped a class, everybody looked right through me like I'd died."
    sera "Di rumah dulu—Chicago, rasanya Chicago deh, dekat danau besar yang dingin—nilaku selalu 99,4, pemain biola utama, lulus awal. Pas satu semester aku tumbang karena depresi dan ngulang satu mata pelajaran, semua orang langsung natap aku kayak orang mati."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:111
translate indonesian chapter2_start_31322245:

    # sera "Here, when I raise my hand, armies cheer. Children paint wooden stars on their doors. ...So why are you looking at me like I'm the one losing, Sato?!"
    sera "Di sini, waktu kuangkat tanganku, seluruh pasukan bersorak. Anak-anak menggambar bintang di pintu rumah mereka. ...Jadi kenapa kau malah natap aku kayak orang yang kalah, Sato?!"

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:121
translate indonesian chapter2_start_d871f680:

    # leo "Lakeshore buses hiss when they kneel at the curb in November rain. Wet brakes, roasted peanuts on State Street, and radiator pipes clanking at five in the morning."
    leo "Bus kota Lakeshore selalu mendesis waktu berhenti di trotoar saat hujan bulan November. Bau rem basah, aroma kacang panggang di State Street, dan bunyi pipa pemanas yang berisik jam lima pagi."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:122
translate indonesian chapter2_start_c44288d0:

    # leo "Nobody deserves to be turned into a lighthouse just because people like the view, Sera. Even if you dropped every sword tomorrow, you'd still be a real person."
    leo "Nggak ada orang yang pantas dijadikan mercusuar cuma karena orang lain suka pemandangannya, Sera. Bahkan kalau besok kamu buang semua pedangmu, kamu tetaplah manusia yang berharga."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:123
translate indonesian chapter2_start_3b3561cc:

    # narrator "Seraphina stands completely still for five seconds. Then she sits down on the opposite end of the stone step, pulls her knees to her chest, and whispers to herself."
    narrator "Seraphina terdiam mematung selama lima detik. Lalu dia duduk di ujung anak tangga batu, memeluk kedua lututnya ke dada, dan berbisik pelan pada dirinya sendiri."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:124
translate indonesian chapter2_start_c42466c1:

    # sera "'Lakeshore buses hiss at the curb...' Don't let me forget that one tomorrow, okay, cubicle guy?"
    sera "'Bus Lakeshore mendesis di trotoar...' Jangan biarkan aku melupakan kalimat itu besok ya, cowok kantoran?"

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:131
translate indonesian chapter2_start_2233bdcd:

    # sera "...God, I hate that you sound like my older sister. Get some sleep, Sato. If you slow me down in the Archive tomorrow, I won't carry you."
    sera "...Astaga, aku benci suaramu yang mirip kakak perempuanku. Tidurlah sana, Sato. Kalau besok kau bikin lambat di Arsip, aku nggak bakal mau nggendong kau ya."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:139
translate indonesian chapter2_start_2703f868:

    # sera "...Careful what you ask for. Hold out your palm."
    sera "...Hati-hati dengan apa yang kau minta. Buka telapak tanganmu."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:142
translate indonesian chapter2_start_1878166a:

    # narrator "Cold violet fire threads into my wrist. Instantly my shoulders feel lighter, sharper, fearless—and when I try to picture the bicycle I rode in third grade, there's only white static."
    narrator "Api dingin violet merayap ke pergelangan tanganku. Seketika bahuku terasa lebih ringan, tajam, tak kenal takut—namun saat kucoba mengingat sepeda yang kukuasai waktu kelas tiga SD dulu, yang tersisa hanya derau putih."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:156
translate indonesian chapter2_start_813baf16:

    # narrator "Before turning in, I find Vespera kneeling at the western salt-bluff with a small iron hammer, driving a brass survey marker into the frost-white crust."
    narrator "Sebelum tidur, kutemukan Vespera sedang berlutut di tebing garam barat dengan palu besi kecil, menancapkan patok ukur kuningan ke tanah beku putih."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:158
translate indonesian chapter2_start_5fece4ea:

    # vespera "My father mapped orchard boundaries across this ridge. Every autumn I move the stake back three inches where Master Orin's compost worms manage to eat the salt."
    vespera "Ayahku dulu memetakan batas kebun apel di sepanjang bukit ini. Tiap musim gugur, kugeser patok ini mundur delapan sentimeter di tempat cacing kompos Kakek Orin berhasil mengikis garamnya."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:160
translate indonesian chapter2_start_5621f231:

    # vespera "Twenty years ago, when the Sixth Hero flew overhead in golden armor, nine-year-old me waved a little paper flag and screamed 'Save us!' Ten minutes later, my parents' apple trees rang like crystal wineglasses and shattered."
    vespera "Dua puluh tahun lalu, waktu Pahlawan Keenam terbang di langit dengan zirah emas, aku yang masih sembilan tahun melambaikan bendera kertas kecil dan teriak 'Selamatkan kami!' Sepuluh menit kemudian, pohon-pohon apel milik orang tuaku berdenting kayak gelas kristal—lalu hancur berkeping-keping."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:161
translate indonesian chapter2_start_21aa17cd:

    # vespera "That's why I pull Outworlders {i}out{/i} of Solvara, Leo. Not because I hate heroes. Because no frightened kid from Earth should ever be handed a button that deletes a valley—or deletes themselves."
    vespera "Itulah alasanku memulangkan para Pendatang {i}keluar{/i} dari Solvara, Leo. Bukan karena aku benci pahlawan. Tapi karena tidak boleh ada anak ketakutan dari Bumi yang disodori tombol untuk melenyapkan satu lembah—atau melenyapkan diri mereka sendiri."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:170
translate indonesian chapter2_start_9c0b67a5:

    # narrator "As my lantern beam grazes the ancient boundary stone beneath Vespera's boots, a familiar glint of mica-glass catches the amber light!"
    narrator "Saat sorot lenteraku menyapu batu batas purba di bawah sepatu bot Vespera, kilau kaca mika yang kukenal menangkap cahaya temaram!"

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:171
translate indonesian chapter2_start_48a21fab:

    # leo "Vespera—hold on! Look wedged inside the old surveyor's benchmark!"
    leo "Vespera—tunggu! Lihat yang terselip di dalam patok ukur tua itu!"

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:172
translate indonesian chapter2_start_17b6f1d0:

    # narrator "Together we lift out a second tiny mica-sealed three-leaf clover, etched on the reverse in faded English: {i}'Root Two: Where orchards remember rain.'{/i}"
    narrator "Bersama-sama kami mengangkat liontin semanggi berdaun tiga kedua yang terbungkus mika, dengan ukiran bahasa Inggris di baliknya: {i}'Akar Dua: Di mana kebun apel mengingat hujan.'{/i}"

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:176
translate indonesian chapter2_start_f16da7bf:

    # vespera "...Four-hundred-year-old First-Era glass. Right on my father's survey line. Keep that safe in your satchel, Leo."
    vespera "...Kaca Era Pertama berusia empat ratus tahun. Tepat di garis ukur mendiang ayahku. Simpan baik-baik di tasmu, Leo."

# game/story/chapter2.rpy:181
translate indonesian chapter2_start_56c93932:

    # vespera "...What even is this fabric, woven frog-skin? It blocks wind better than oiled wool. ...Thanks, Question-Mark."
    vespera "...Kain apa sih ini sebenarnya, rajutan kulit kodok? Bisa nahan angin lebih bagus daripada wol minyak. ...Makasih ya, Si Tanda Tanya."

translate indonesian strings:

    # game/story/chapter2.rpy:50
    old "Quietly say, \"Lemon. With a spoonful of cheap honey in a chipped mug.\" (Without pity or smugness)"
    new "Ucapkan pelan, \"Lemon. Ditambah sesendok madu murah di dalam cangkir yang gompal.\" (Tanpa nada kasihan atau jumawa)"

    # game/story/chapter2.rpy:59
    old "Confront Marshal Cassian directly: \"You see what that magic is doing to her! You can't feed another person to a furnace!\""
    new "Hadapi Marsekal Cassian secara langsung: \"Anda lihat sendiri apa yang diperbuat sihir itu padanya! Anda tidak bisa mengumpankan satu orang lagi ke dalam tungku api!\""

    # game/story/chapter2.rpy:66
    old "Study Cassian's map and ask Vespera: \"Wait—if the Aqueduct copper-spade grounded a small seam, couldn't a bigger array ground Bastion?\""
    new "Pelajari peta Cassian lalu tanya Vespera: \"Tunggu—kalau sekop tembaga di Akuaduk bisa membumikan celah kecil, bukankah rangkaian yang lebih besar bisa membumikan Benteng Bastion?\""

    # game/story/chapter2.rpy:114
    old "Sit on the wet step six feet away and describe the sound of rain on Chicago asphalt—and tell her she doesn't owe anyone her whole mind."
    new "Duduk di undakan basah berjarak dua meter darinya dan lukiskan suara hujan di atas aspal Chicago—serta katakan bahwa dia tak berutang seluruh isi kepalanya kepada siapa pun."

    # game/story/chapter2.rpy:126
    old "Tell her bluntly: \"Because applause isn't warmth, Sera. Look at those statues in town—nobody visits a monument once the war's over.\""
    new "Katakan terus terang padanya: \"Karena tepuk tangan bukanlah kehangatan, Sera. Lihatlah patung-patung di kota itu—tak ada yang mengunjungi monumen setelah perang usai.\""

    # game/story/chapter2.rpy:133
    old "\"Teach me how you channel Starlight. Even a little. If things go wrong tomorrow, a garden spade won't be enough.\""
    new "\"Ajari aku cara menyalurkan Cahaya Bintang. Sedikit saja. Kalau besok keadaan memburuk, sekop kebun tak akan cukup.\""

    # game/story/chapter2.rpy:168
    old "Help her steady the lantern—and inspect the carved stone protruding beside the old orchard marker."
    new "Bantu dia memegangi lentera agar tetap tenang—lalu periksa batu berukir yang menyembul di sebelah patok kebun buah tua itu."

    # game/story/chapter2.rpy:178
    old "Take off my olive windbreaker and drape it over her shivering shoulders while she finishes hammering the stake."
    new "Lepaskan jaket angin hijau zaitunku dan sampirkan ke bahunya yang menggigil selagi dia menyelesaikan ketukan pada patok itu."

